<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>Except as provided in Sections 1689.6 to 1689.11, inclusive, within 10 days after a home solicitation contract or offer has been canceled, the seller must tender to the buyer any payments made by the buyer and any note or other evidence of indebtedness.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>If the downpayment includes goods traded in, the goods must be tendered in substantially as good condition as when received.</p><p>(c)<span class="EnSpace"/>Until the seller has complied with the obligations imposed by Sections 1689.7 to 1689.11, inclusive, the buyer may retain possession
of goods delivered to him by the seller and has a lien on the goods for any recovery to which he is entitled.</p></caml:Content>